# Builder spec truth — implementation report

**Status: DONE.** All acceptance criteria met, full suite green, nothing weakened, no product UI changed, nothing staged/committed.

## Chair decision (CD-8 — in-contract, not escalated)

I held this decision. Options enumerated and chosen:

| Question | Options | Chosen | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| Block flow (fact 3) | `hero` / `richtext` / `card-grid` / `quote` / `cta` (the only shipped blocks, `storage/cms-themes/akira-editorial/block-definitions.json:5,54,85,144,175`) | **`richtext`** | The original intent was a *heading* section (`+ heading`). `richtext.title` is the shipped heading primitive — it renders `<h2>` — and its `body` lets the preview prove content. `hero` is a page-level layout section, not a heading; the other three are not headings. |
| Route for the string `"Composition editor"` | assert on list route (impossible) / assert on editor route | **editor route** | `app.tsx:52` selects the panel from `boot.mode`; list mode renders `<h2>Compositions</h2>` (`app.tsx:80`) and the string exists only in `EditPanel` (`app.tsx:435`). List-route assertions now name what `ListPanel` truly ships (`app.tsx:80,84`). |
| Publish fixture | use a random key / reuse an existing post / create a published fixture | **create a deterministic published fixture, delete it in `finally`** | `akira.builder.publish@1` resolves the post via `akira.post.get@1`, which only returns `status='published'` posts (`cms-akira-core/helpers/capabilities.php:209`), else 422 (`cms-akira-builder/helpers.php:903`). The original random key named no post, so publish was unreachable. Reusing an existing post is not deterministic. |
| BaseURL precedence | `APP_URL` first / `TENANT_URL` first | **`TENANT_URL` first** | `.env` sets `APP_URL=http://ikabudsix.test` (kernel/control host) and `TENANT_URL=http://akiracms.test`. The builder's `/cms-akira-shell/*` routes 404 on the kernel host (verified: kernel `404`, tenant `200`), so a relative `goto` must resolve to the tenant. |

No L4 was triggered; all decisions stayed inside the contract.

## S1 — spec rewrite (`tests/browser/akira-builder-admin.spec.ts`)

Journey now executes end to end and asserts the shipped UI:

```
shell session (from auth.setup storageState, no login POST)
→ create published post fixture (UI + governed workflow submit→approve→publish)
→ open builder LIST via a relative goto → 200 + tenant origin
→ assert ListPanel: heading "Compositions" + "Attach a composition to a post"
→ click the real "Compose “<title>”" link → editor route
→ assert EditPanel: heading "Composition editor"
→ fill title, select real block richtext, fill heading + body, "+ Add Rich text"
→ Create & save draft → control flips to "Save draft"
→ server-rendered preview iframe contains the authored <h2> and body
→ Validate → ".ab-ok" contains "Validated"
→ Publish (confirm dialog) → .ab-pill-pub = PUBLISHED + "published revision N"
→ return to list → the composition row shows PUBLISHED
→ finally: delete composition + soft-delete post
```

The previous run's corrections (storageState auth, absolute URLs) were kept and are recorded. Nothing was deleted from the journey; `validate` was already a step and now runs.

## S2 — baseURL precedence fix (`playwright.config.js`)

```diff
-        // APP_URL wins; TENANT_URL is the name the specs themselves use. The default
+        // TENANT_URL wins; APP_URL is the kernel/control host in .env. The default
         // is the tenant host these specs actually drive -- the previous default
-        // (palsystem.test) is stale, and because the Akira specs use relative
-        // page.goto() it made them impossible to run under this config.
-        baseURL: process.env.APP_URL || process.env.TENANT_URL || 'http://akiracms.test',
+        // (palsystem.test) is stale, and a relative page.goto() must resolve to the
+        // tenant (the builder's /cms-akira-shell/* routes 404 on the kernel host),
+        // not to whichever host APP_URL happens to name.
+        baseURL: process.env.TENANT_URL || process.env.APP_URL || 'http://akiracms.test',
```

