| 2 | `page.goto('/cms-akira-shell/compositions/${key}/edit')` (relative) | `.env` `APP_URL=http://ikabudsix.test`; config preferred `APP_URL`; kernel route `404` vs tenant `200` | resolved to the kernel host → 404 → no builder root | config prefers `TENANT_URL`; the first builder nav is relative and asserts `200` + tenant origin | the builder journey is reachable from the configured baseURL |
| 3 | `click('button:has-text("+ heading")')` | `block-definitions.json:54` etc. (no `heading` block); `app.tsx:497` renders `+ Add {label}` | no such block and the text never matches | select `richtext`, `+ Add Rich text`, canvas contains `Rich text` + heading | a real validated theme block is added |
| 4 | after save, `.ab-ok,.ab-error` contains `/Created\|Saved/` | `app.tsx:244` sets the toast; `app.tsx:251` calls `reload()`; `app.tsx:171` does `setResult(null)` | the save handler clears its own toast, so it is not reliably observable | Save control flips to `Save draft` **and** the server-rendered preview contains the authored heading/body | the draft persisted and renders server-side |
| 5 | attach to random key `pw-<ts>`, then Publish | `cms-akira-builder/helpers.php:901-903` requires `akira.post.get@1`; `capabilities.php:209` returns published posts only | the key names no post → publish 422; original never created a post | deterministic published post fixture, attach by slug, then publish | a composition attached to a real published post is published |
| 6 | `#cms-akira-builder-root input` first (positional) | — (worked, but brittle) | not impossible; positional | `getByLabel('Title').first()` + `.ab-block-form`-scoped block props | same authored values persisted |
| 7 | click `Render preview (draft)`, iframe visible | — (worked; save auto-renders) | not impossible; redundant | iframe visible + `frameLocator` asserts the rendered heading and body | the saved server-rendered draft is shown |
| 8 | Publish → `.ab-pill-pub` = `PUBLISHED` | — (unreachable via #5) | blocked by #5, not by the assertion | kept, now reachable; plus the published row on the list route | published state visible in editor and in persisted list |

Nothing is asserted weaker than the original intent. Where the original proved a *toast*, the spec now proves the *persisted revision + server render* (strictly stronger); where it proved a *pill*, it still proves the pill and additionally the list projection.

## S4 — product findings (recorded, not absorbed)

**PF-1 — the save confirmation is cleared before the user can read it.** `handleSave` sets `Created draft composition.` / `Saved draft revision.` (`app.tsx:244,248`) and then immediately `await reload()` (`app.tsx:251`); `reload()`'s first statement is `setResult(null)` (`app.tsx:171`). React can batch these into one render, so the success message is not reliably visible. Evidence: `modules/cms-akira/cms-akira-builder/admin-ui/src/app.tsx:171,244,251`. This did **not** block the journey, and I did **not** weaken the save check to accommodate it — the spec asserts the durable result (revision exists, preview renders). Recorded here as required.

**Reviewed, not a defect:** the editor allows a composition key to be created/saved/validated before the post exists or is published; the failure only surfaces at publish (422). This matches the product's draft-first model and the list only offers existing posts, so it is noted, not filed.

## S5 — robustness

- No `waitForTimeout`; no `test.skip` / `test.fail` / `test.fixme` / `describe.skip` (grep: `NONE FOUND`).
- Assertions use `getByRole`/`getByLabel`/`getByText` and retrying `expect` with auto-wait; `waitForURL` for navigation.
- The one timing-dependent relationship (post fixture must be published before the composition can publish) is made deterministic by awaiting the workflow state, not by sleeping.

